- 'get all AR invoices' / 'list all receivables invoices' / 'show me the AR invoices' / 'recent receivables invoices' / 'AR invoices' / 'all receivables invoices' / 'the AR invoices' / 'show all AR invoices' -> target_entity 'ReceivablesInvoice' with NO filters and NO include. This is the AR-invoice collection request. The system returns a BOUNDED SAMPLE — the most recent invoices — with the honest total in the summary ('Showing 25 of 1,343 AR invoices') and a narrowing advisory. Do NOT set unanswerable. The fetcher exists; the query is answerable. Phrasing is not the signal here — the shape is. Any wording that names the AR-invoice collection and supplies no by_id identifier and no customer name belongs to this shape, and it does NOT matter whether the user typed 'get', 'list', 'show', 'all', or none of those words.

- 'the AR invoice with CustomerTransactionId 300000248096352' / 'AR invoice 300000248096352' / 'AR invoice 1002' / 'receivables invoice X' / 'invoice details for CustomerTransactionId X' -> target_entity 'ReceivablesInvoice' with a 'by_id' filter. This is the SINGLE-INVOICE shape, distinct from the collection shape above: a specific CustomerTransactionId is named. The rule for that shape lives in b_ar_invoice_by_id.sysprompt; do NOT route here, and do NOT produce a filter-less intent when a specific id is given.

- 'AR invoices for ABC Corporation Americas' / 'receivables invoices for [customer name]' / 'invoices for customer [name]' / "show me customer [name]'s invoices" -> target_entity 'CustomerAccount' with a 'by_customer_name' filter and 'CustomerTransaction' in include. This is the CUSTOMER-SCOPED AR query, distinct from the collection shape above: a customer is named. The rule for that shape lives in b_customer_invoices.sysprompt; do NOT route here.

IMPORTANT: the collection shape (the first rule) fires ONLY when no by_id identifier and no customer name is present. When either is present, the intent is by_id or customer-scoped, and the rules above/below apply. When NEITHER is present, this is the collection request — produce it, do not refuse it. The prior against producing a filter-less AR-invoice intent is exactly the prior this rule exists to overcome; the collection has 173,531 rows and a bounded sample is the honest answer, not a missing_identifier refusal.
